<!--
  accountActivation as MJML -- a spike, not a source.

  accountActivation/html.pug stays the source of truth; this file is here to be
  opened in a split-screen preview (VS Code: "MJML Official", Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+P ->
  "MJML: Preview") so the table-based, Outlook-safe output can be looked at next to
  the div-based one the pug templates produce today. Nothing reads it:
  tools/extract.mjs takes html.pug and subject.pug from each template DIRECTORY, so
  a file sitting here beside those directories is inert to the build.

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  SETTINGS -- one, and only because MJML 5 sandboxes mj-include:

      "mjml.allowIncludes": true

  Without it the preview silently drops header and footer: a denied include leaves
  a "mj-include denied" comment in the output and no error at all.

  There is deliberately no "mjml.includePath" to go with it. What MJML allows by
  default is the directory of the file being compiled and its subdirectories --
  which is exactly why this file lives HERE, beside includes/, rather than one
  level down in accountActivation/. From there every include would cross out of
  its own directory and each one would need the templates root declared as an
  extra allowed root, in the editor and again in every script.

  From a script or the CLI the setting is `ignoreIncludes: false`, and nothing
  else. Should a template ever need a partial from outside this tree, that is when
  `includePath` comes in -- absolute, because at library level a relative entry is
  resolved against the compiled FILE's directory, and one that does not resolve is
  dropped in silence.
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Everything shared lives in includes/ and is edited once:

      head.mjml      the theme -- fonts, sizes, colours, mj-class, mj-style,
                     and the mj-body defaults. A design change is THIS file.
      top.mjml       everything above the content   -> header.mjml
      bottom.mjml    everything below the content   -> greeting.mjml, footer.mjml
                                                       footer.mjml -> social.mjml

  What stays per template is the six-line skeleton below plus the content that
  makes this mail this mail.

  The text below IS English, not a key standing in for it -- gettext, the way
  packages/frontend writes `t.__('Sign in')`. Catalogues are ../po/<lang>/messages.po.
  Two markers, and .mjmlconfig.js resolves both for the preview:

    {{t:Activate account}}           the message. Untranslated, it stays English
    {{t:Hello %1 %2,|first,last}}    %1/%2 filled from the slots named after the |
    {{v:activationLink}}             a slot on its own

  In the build the first becomes the catalogue string for the locale and the
  second becomes a SENTINEL, which is what makes the slot a slot:

    marker                     preview            build              ships as
    -----------------------    ---------------    ----------------   ------------
    {{t:Hello %1 %2,|...}}     "Hallo Max M.,"    "Hallo " + slots   pool bytes
    {{v:activationLink}}       the sample URL     U+0001..U+0002     a slot op

  Reading the source is therefore reading the mail, with no tooling in the way --
  that is the whole point of the English-as-msgid form. A missing translation
  degrades to this text rather than to a key or a blank.

  Your language for the preview is ../.preview-locale (gitignored), or MJML_LOCALE
  for one run. The sample values are ../.preview-values.json, and putting a
  40-character surname in there is the point of that file.

  Slots used below: firstName, lastName, activationLink, resendLink, hours, and
  logoUrl in the branch that is commented out.
-->
<!-- lang= is layout.pug's html(lang=locale): a slot the RENDERER fills from the
     locale it was called with, not one a caller supplies -- which is why it does
     not show up in the struct. -->
<mjml lang="{{v:locale}}">
  <mj-head>
    <mj-include path="includes/head.mjml" />
    <mj-title>{{t:Email Verification}}</mj-title>
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body>
    <mj-include path="includes/top.mjml" />

    <!--@if logoUrl-->
    <mj-section padding="20px 25px 0 25px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="{{v:logoUrl}}" alt="Banner" border-radius="20px" padding="0" />
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!--@endif-->

    <mj-section padding="15px 25px 0 25px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text mj-class="h2">{{t:Email Verification}}</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- .text-block + includes/salutation.pug -->
    <mj-section padding="20px 25px 0 25px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text mj-class="muted">{{t:Hello %1 %2,|firstName,lastName}}</mj-text>
        <mj-text mj-class="muted">{{t:Your email address has just been registered with Gradido.}}</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- .content: the grey card. mj-wrapper is what carries a border and a
         radius around several sections; mj-section cannot nest in mj-section. -->
    <mj-wrapper
      background-color="#f5f5f5"
      border="1px solid #808080"
      border-radius="24px"
      padding="20px 8% 40px 8%"
      css-class="card"
    >
      <mj-section background-color="#f5f5f5">
        <mj-column>
          <mj-text mj-class="h2" padding="20px 0 0 0">{{t:Complete registration}}</mj-text>
          <mj-text mj-class="p-content" padding="15px 0 15px 0">
            {{t:Please click here to complete the registration and activate your Gradido account.}}
          </mj-text>

          <!-- .button-3, the gold one: "the way on to wherever the thing lives" -->
          <mj-button
            mj-class="btn"
            css-class="btn-gold"
            background-color="#c58d38"
            href="{{v:activationLink}}"
          >{{t:Activate account}}</mj-button>

          <mj-text mj-class="p-content" padding="15px 0 15px 0">
            {{t:Or copy the link into your browser window.}}
          </mj-text>

          <!-- .clink -->
          <mj-text mj-class="p-content" css-class="clink" padding="0 0 40px 0">
            <a href="{{v:activationLink}}" style="color:#696c72;">{{v:activationLink}}</a>
          </mj-text>

          <mj-include path="includes/request-new-link.mjml" />
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>
    </mj-wrapper>

    <mj-include path="includes/bottom.mjml" />
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
